1. assignment is an expression:   r = (b.x = 5)         -> r is 5, b.x is 5 (the body's :ignored is discarded)
2. the body's value via send:     b.send(:x=, 6)        -> :ignored; b.method(:x=).call(7) -> :ignored
3. attr_writer:                   (b.w = 3)             -> 3; b.w -> NoMethodError: undefined method 'w' for an instance of Box
4. two values on the right:       b.x = 1, 2; b.x       -> [1, 2] (an Array)
5. inside the class, self is required: b.set_wrong(50)  -> 50, b.x still [1, 2]; b.set_right(60) -> 60, b.x now 60
6. chained assignment:            a = b.x = 9           -> a is 9, b.x is 9
7. []= too:                       (b[:k] = "v")         -> "v"; b.send(:[]=, :k2, "v2") -> :ignored_too
8. += and ||= go through the pair: (b.x += 1)           -> 10, b.x is 10; (Box.new.x ||= 100) -> 100
9. no universal hook:             bag.color = "red"     -> "red" via method_missing; bag.stored -> {color: "red"}; bag.send(:color=, "blue") -> :ignored_three
